  "completed": [
    "Guardian v1 remains byte-for-byte unchanged. The versioned successor reuses its frozen runtime, cgroup, release, pidfd, poll and retirement primitives.",
    "One exact CgroupLease and one exact release descriptor enter a private authority bundle through a callback-free constructor. Its one-shot take clears both references before returning them and exposes only aggregate consumed, failed and caller-retention state.",
    "Runtime, scalar-argument and guardian-lock rejection occur before bundle consumption. The caller therefore retains both authorities on those paths without inspecting an exception code.",
    "After bundle consumption, the guardian records ownership before calling lease verification or release-descriptor validation. Every later failure attempts one lease retirement and one release-descriptor close; caller cleanup is forbidden even if cleanup cannot be confirmed.",
    "A release descriptor whose identity has not yet been captured is still closed once because the exact numeric descriptor was explicitly transferred. After identity capture, replacement is rejected and an ambiguous close is never retried.",
    "The predecessor reason priority, release send, cgroup retirement, generation-stable broker stop and owned pidfd cleanup remain unchanged. The borrowed broker pidfd is never closed.",
    "Public execution remains closed and all unproved process-topology, origin, receipt, native-enforcement, execution, import and training claims remain false."
  ],
  "authority_contract": {
    "preconsumption_caller_retains_lease_and_release_fd": true,
    "postconsumption_caller_retains_lease_and_release_fd": false,
    "ownership_decided_from_exception_code": false,
    "validation_callbacks_before_consumption": 0,
